course: dictionary
lesson: 9904
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Talkie is a noun, and it has two meanings. The old-fashioned one is a film with sound and spoken words. The other is found inside the word walkie-talkie. To choose the right meaning, look at the clues around the word.
explain: «A walkie-talkie sends your voice by radio straight to another walkie-talkie with no masts, and only one person can talk at a time, so people say over when they finish.» The clues are radio, voice and talk, so this is the small hand-held radio meaning.
explain: Talkies are old films with sound, and the clues would be cinema, screens or history lessons. Ask yourself: is this text about films or about radios? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A talkie is a film with sound and spoken words.
fact: Before talkies, films were silent, and words appeared on cards on the screen.
fact: When talkies came, many silent film stars lost their jobs.
fact: A walkie-talkie is a small hand-held radio for talking to someone nearby.
fact: On a walkie-talkie, people say over when they finish, because only one person can talk at a time.
exercise: «The first talkies were made a long time ago.» What is a talkie? | A film with no sound at all | *A film with sound and spoken words | A small radio for talking to someone nearby
exercise: Ella hears, «Pass me the walkie-talkie, I'm at the top of the hill.» What does walkie-talkie mean? | A tall tower that sends pictures | A type of camping tent | *A small hand-held radio for talking to someone nearby
exercise: «Many silent film stars lost their jobs when the talkies came.» Find and copy one word that means a film with no sound. | jobs | came | *silent | stars
test: «Our walkie-talkies crackled, so we said over when we finished.» Why do people say over? | To say goodbye for ever | Because the radio is broken | *So the other person knows it is their turn to talk
test: «Grandpa loved the old talkies from the 1930s.» What does talkies mean here? | Hand-held radios for talking nearby | *Films with sound and spoken words | Cameras that take photos of people
exam: «Walkie-talkies crackled in the tent, and the guard spoke into his.» Which meaning of talkie fits walkie-talkie here? | A type of tent | A map of the campsite | *A small radio for talking to someone nearby | A film with spoken words
